# Build context for Dockerfile.development.
#
# BuildKit uses `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` INSTEAD of the root `.dockerignore`
# when it exists, so this file is the dev build's complete list -- it does not
# layer on top of `.dockerignore`. The two are near-copies on purpose: the only
# difference is `.devcontainer`, which the root file excludes (nothing in the
# production image reads it, and `Dockerfile`'s `COPY . /home/user/app/` would
# otherwise ship shell dotfiles to ECS) but this build needs, because
# Dockerfile.development copies `setup.sh` + `config-files/` and runs them to
# build the zsh/oh-my-posh shell `make bash` drops you into.
#
# Keep the rest in sync with `.dockerignore` when you edit either one.

.db
node_modules
npm-debug.log
.venv
.git
.github
.claude
.mailpit-data
ai-plans
ai-tools
docs
infrastructure
junit
staticfiles
mediafiles
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.env
.env.docker

# Local AI-tooling state: worktrees, caches and PR-context staging. Untracked,
# hundreds of megabytes, and read by nothing inside either image.
.vinta-ai-maestro
.vinta-ai-workflows

# Test support. Excluded here only to keep the context small -- the development
# image gets all of it back through the compose bind mount
# (`./:/home/user/app/`), which is what `make test` runs against. See the longer
# note in `.dockerignore` for why the production image must not ship these.
**/tests
**/testing
**/factories.py
**/fixtures.py
conftest.py
